1
00:00:00,760 --> 00:00:01,930
English tenses.

2
00:00:02,140 --> 00:00:06,010
This is something most of the students have often trouble with.

3
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,290
What terms to use.

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:11,380
How to make a correct sentence.

5
00:00:11,680 --> 00:00:19,270
Let's have a look at the most popular English tenses and situations when we use those tenses.

6
00:00:19,630 --> 00:00:20,710
Let's go.

7
00:00:20,890 --> 00:00:21,880
Present.

8
00:00:21,880 --> 00:00:22,840
Simple.

9
00:00:23,050 --> 00:00:24,520
I do.

10
00:00:24,550 --> 00:00:26,350
She does.

11
00:00:26,710 --> 00:00:32,540
We use present simple when we describe or introduce ourselves.

12
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,680
For example, my name is Kate.

13
00:00:36,550 --> 00:00:38,650
I live with my family.

14
00:00:38,830 --> 00:00:42,700
I work as an English teacher and so on.

15
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:48,100
Also, we use Present Simple to talk about our daily routine.

16
00:00:48,130 --> 00:00:53,080
For example, I wake up at 8:00 in the morning.

17
00:00:53,110 --> 00:01:01,940
I usually drink coffee in the morning or I have a daily meeting at 10 a.m..

18
00:01:02,360 --> 00:01:10,410
Also, we can use Present Simple to talk about things that we like or things that we hate.

19
00:01:10,430 --> 00:01:13,070
For example, I like pizza.

20
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,070
I like English.

21
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:20,780
I like to watch movies or I don't like this idea.

22
00:01:20,780 --> 00:01:25,040
I am not a big fan of this sport and so on.

23
00:01:25,190 --> 00:01:31,160
We use present simple with words like every day.

24
00:01:31,190 --> 00:01:32,180
Often.

25
00:01:32,210 --> 00:01:33,200
Usually.

26
00:01:33,200 --> 00:01:35,870
Sometimes on Mondays.

27
00:01:35,900 --> 00:01:37,850
Every weekend.

28
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,430
Present continuous.

29
00:01:41,180 --> 00:01:43,460
I am doing.

30
00:01:43,490 --> 00:01:46,130
She is doing.

31
00:01:46,670 --> 00:01:53,470
We use this tense to talk about things that we are doing at this moment.

32
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:56,030
For example, I am speaking.

33
00:01:56,030 --> 00:01:57,980
You are listening.

34
00:01:57,980 --> 00:01:59,390
I am teaching.

35
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:01,460
You are studying.

36
00:02:01,850 --> 00:02:02,900
All right.

37
00:02:02,900 --> 00:02:06,600
So it is often used with words like.

38
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:12,050
Now at this moment as we speak right now.

39
00:02:12,490 --> 00:02:13,980
For example.

40
00:02:13,990 --> 00:02:15,100
I'm sorry.

41
00:02:15,100 --> 00:02:21,010
I cannot talk to you right now because I am writing an important email.

42
00:02:21,790 --> 00:02:27,850
Also, we can use present continuous to talk about events in the future.

43
00:02:27,850 --> 00:02:32,340
Something that we planned some arrangements.

44
00:02:32,350 --> 00:02:37,750
For example, I am meeting Tom at two.

45
00:02:38,290 --> 00:02:41,350
I am having a lunch with Kelly.

46
00:02:43,230 --> 00:02:46,650
I am planning to see this film.

47
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:48,990
Future Simple.

48
00:02:49,560 --> 00:02:50,790
I will work.

49
00:02:50,910 --> 00:02:52,920
She will work.

50
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:57,750
We use this tense to talk about something In the future.

51
00:02:57,750 --> 00:03:02,550
For example, I will be able to meet you at five.

52
00:03:02,580 --> 00:03:11,160
She will work on this task after she finishes her current task so we can use it to talk about events

53
00:03:11,160 --> 00:03:12,720
happening in the future.

54
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:18,840
Often used with words like tomorrow in a couple of hours in the future.

55
00:03:19,740 --> 00:03:20,820
Next month.

56
00:03:20,850 --> 00:03:22,050
Next year.

57
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:23,960
Past.

58
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,010
Simple.

59
00:03:26,040 --> 00:03:27,930
I worked.

60
00:03:28,200 --> 00:03:30,360
She worked.

61
00:03:31,350 --> 00:03:38,280
They say, okay, we used past simple to talk about things that happened in the past.

62
00:03:38,730 --> 00:03:39,330
Okay.

63
00:03:39,330 --> 00:03:47,270
It is often used with words like yesterday, last month, last year, two days ago.

64
00:03:47,280 --> 00:03:51,940
So we often indicate when this happened.

65
00:03:51,960 --> 00:03:53,940
We often use time.

66
00:03:54,270 --> 00:04:01,800
For example, I worked on this project last year.

67
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:08,160
I worked for this company two years ago.

68
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:14,490
I studied Python few months ago.

69
00:04:15,300 --> 00:04:24,630
We often use it to talk about our past experience, our past company, our past projects and so on.

70
00:04:24,630 --> 00:04:31,230
So, for example, during the job interview, you may use this tense to talk about your previous company,

71
00:04:31,230 --> 00:04:34,260
previous project and responsibilities.

72
00:04:34,860 --> 00:04:36,510
Present Perfect.

73
00:04:37,230 --> 00:04:39,630
I have finished the task.

74
00:04:39,900 --> 00:04:42,870
She has finished the task.

75
00:04:42,960 --> 00:04:47,190
We use present Perfect to talk about the result.

76
00:04:47,220 --> 00:04:51,300
For example, I can show you this project.

77
00:04:51,300 --> 00:04:53,850
I have finally completed it.

78
00:04:54,360 --> 00:04:58,110
Also, we can use it to talk about our experience.

79
00:04:58,440 --> 00:05:02,290
I have worked with this framework.

80
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:10,030
I have worked with this technology or I haven't worked with this technology before.

81
00:05:10,060 --> 00:05:13,790
We can ask someone if they have experience with something.

82
00:05:13,810 --> 00:05:18,160
For example, have you ever worked with JavaScript?

83
00:05:18,310 --> 00:05:25,540
We can also use it to say about how long we worked for a company or a project.

84
00:05:25,540 --> 00:05:30,970
For example, I have worked in this company for two years.

85
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:44,070
I have worked in this company since 2020, so present perfect is often used with the words already yet

86
00:05:44,070 --> 00:05:47,190
just since four.

87
00:05:48,560 --> 00:05:54,560
She has worked here since 2019.

88
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:58,310
She has worked here for two years.

89
00:05:58,490 --> 00:06:01,310
She has finished the task.

90
00:06:01,340 --> 00:06:04,100
She hasn't finished the task yet.

91
00:06:04,460 --> 00:06:13,670
Now, you know the most popular English tenses and you can use them to talk about your everyday life,

92
00:06:13,700 --> 00:06:22,580
your experience, your plans, things that you are doing right now and your accomplishments and results.

93
00:06:23,210 --> 00:06:23,900
Thank you.
